%!PS
% SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 EfterScript contributors
% SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
% backend: none
% expect-output: abc
% expect-output: 0
% expect-output: abc
% expect-output: 5
% Scenario: a reusable stream is read twice. The string becomes a
% positionable file: the first read yields the bytes, a read at the end
% yields nothing but leaves the file open, resetfile takes it back to
% the start for a second read, and a stream over the job's own data is
% made the same way, read through its hexadecimal pre-filter to the
% marker so the program continues after it. The structuring comments
% bound the data for tools that scan the file rather than run it.
% Expect: abc, 0, abc, 5.
(abc) /ReusableStreamDecode filter
dup 10 string readstring pop =
dup 10 string readstring pop length =
dup resetfile 10 string readstring pop =
%%BeginData: 2 ASCII Lines
currentfile << /Filter /ASCIIHexDecode >> /ReusableStreamDecode filter
48656C6C6F>
%%EndData
bytesavailable =
